+
+Fix I would make: use `SafeERC20` for approvals too. With OpenZeppelin v5, prefer `forceApprove` for USDT-compatible approval handling, or approve once during initialization using a USDT-safe zero-then-set pattern. Keep the fork test as a regression test.
+
+## Finding 2: withdrawal fees are stranded instead of accruing to remaining shareholders
+
+Severity: High.
+
+The contract comment says both fees stay supplied in Aave and accrue to remaining shareholders. Withdrawal does not do that. `withdraw()` computes `grossAssets`, deducts a withdrawal fee, subtracts `grossAssets` from `totalAssetsStored`, but only withdraws `netAssets` from Aave (`src/UsdtYieldVault.sol:111-119`). The fee remains as aUSDT, but it is no longer counted by vault accounting. Remaining shareholders do not get it in `balanceOfUnderlying`.
+
+Command:
+
+```sh
+forge test --match-contract UsdtYieldVaultAccountingFailureTest --match-test test_WithdrawalFeesAccrueToRemainingShareholders
+```
+
+Output:
+
+```text
